    "body": "## Independent exact-head review - Chat03B2 atomic participant SQL transition fence\n\n**Exact HEAD reviewed:** `a7314d5eac46fda46af63f10b3a82888612dd3ff`; tree `2ee330c62455c1699c1bdb4cb065b75c31da3f98`, first parent local checkpoint `d6d54031a7bf6c829f133f2c2ba3f1bfad5277f2`. Draft PR #444 remains OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, mergeable clean, and exactly **2 commits** ahead / 0 behind its exact Draft PR #443 base `c0e6ccb11d8302b1e6f7095a063d5c93f5313f98`. Exactly 4 expected files changed: `gameplay-server/migrations/0005_participant_transition_fence.sql`, `gameplay-server/src/worker.js`, `gameplay-server/test/private_api_local_test.mjs`, `gameplay-server/test/test_chat03b2_participant_fence_sql.py`.\n\n**Verdict: `PASS_NARROW_LOCAL_PARTICIPANT_SQL_AUTH_FENCE` / NOT CREDENTIAL-LIFECYCLE OR HOSTED/DEPLOYMENT APPROVAL.** Direct source inspection confirms `gameplay_apply_participant_transition` INSTEAD OF INSERT trigger verifies battle, side, token SHA-256, `status='active'`, generation, and participant identity then inserts into existing `gameplay_apply_transition` within the same SQLite statement. Existing gameplay CAS, receipt and outbox checks are retained. Worker participant commits are switched to fenced view; scheduler `applySystem()` retains internal unrestricted SQL view and public HTTP routes do not select the scheduler path. Authorized GET and stored participant receipt reads use joined/EXISTS active capability + generation checks within one SELECT.\n\n**Exact-head GitHub Actions independently verified against real run metadata/jobs/logs:** [Private Gameplay API #39968710333](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39968710333) SUCCESS, local isolated Wrangler/workerd/D1 test log explicitly reports `D1 migrations 0001 through 0005 and local fixtures`, stale generation rejection with no state/receipt/outbox writes, revoked read/replay denial, concurrent revoke/commit serialized outcomes, legitimate A/B commits and trusted reveal/expire, restart/replay. [CAS SQL #39968709930](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39968709930) SUCCESS, 50/50 Python discovery incl 4 new participant fence tests; [Forensics #39968709949](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39968709949) SUCCESS. Local Codex Wrangler 4.152.0/workerd 1.20261019.1 and 17/17 policy validation reported, but were not separately run by this reviewer.\n\n**Important limits, retained as explicit blockers to release:** Existing `0003` admin create idempotent replay still decrypts original capabilities, even if revoked; it is NOT gated by current capability issuance status/generation and must be closed in a coordinated creation-recovery lifecycle migration before any hosted/real-player use. Historical `generation=1` means schema initialization only. There is no implemented trusted rotate/revoke/admin policy and status can be reset to active by privileged SQL. The unrestricted SQL system transition has no DB-level scheduler authentication; the trusted Worker-only binding and routing remain the security boundary. Authorized GET and receipt SELECT and subsequent response delivery can race a revoke; SQL linearization does not cancel previously authorized HTTP responses.\n\n**Additional hardening observation:** `commit()` currently does one `storedParticipantReceipt()` authorized SQL read, then uses unguarded `load()` for replay view or fresh-command lifecycle examination; a revoke between initial `authorizePlayer()`/authorized receipt lookup and this later unguarded read can cause a 409 (`ALREADY_COMMITTED`, etc.) that reveals limited state-derived information rather than uniformly rejecting the now revoked caller. No unauthorized DB write is possible because the fenced INSERT rechecks atomically. Not a blocker for this narrowly scoped SQL **write** fence, but before any claim of full post-revoke read isolation, replace these unguarded participant reads with appropriately authorized one-statement reads and negative race tests. Preserve valid post-commit in-flight response semantics.\n\nNo hosted Cloudflare/D1 deployment, real participants, main merge, or parent Draft PR merge authorized. Checkpoint + Recovery governance from canonical Notion remains in force. Next independent atom must tackle closed/expired encrypted creation recovery and trusted credential lifecycle with carefully scoped changes and local-only acceptance before deployment approval.",
