    "body": "## Scope\n\nAdd a participant SQL authorization fence for the existing gameplay CAS transition, stacked directly on Draft PR #443 at `c0e6ccb11d8302b1e6f7095a063d5c93f5313f98`.\n\nOnly the migration, Worker routing, and scoped tests are changed. Participant commits validate battle, side, capability digest, active status, and expected generation in the protected SQL state transition. Scheduler reveal/expire remains on Worker-only routing; public HTTP requests cannot select the system path.\n\n## Local evidence\n\n- Wrangler 4.152.0 with workerd 1.20261019.1; actual isolated local D1 executed migrations 0001 through 0005.\n- Local Worker/D1 private API integration PASS, including A/B commits, stale generation, revoked status and replay denial, no-write rejection, concurrent revoke/commit serial outcomes, duplicate receipt behavior, restart/replay, rollback, and trusted scheduler reveal/expire.\n- Python discovery 50/50; offline safety 27/27; policy tests 17/17; repository policy validator, syntax checks, and `git diff --check` PASS.\n\n## Remaining lifecycle block\n\nNo deployment authorization is implied. Existing 0003 encrypted creation-recovery replay still needs coordinated lifecycle closure. Historical generation 1 does not prove credential issuance. Identity, keyring, retention, recovery, revoke/rotation lifecycle decisions remain open. Read/replay responses can still race revocation after the atomic authorization snapshot. Hosted D1, deployment, and real-player access were not used.\n",
